{
  "about": "HellDescent music manifest v1 (2026-10-18). Load as a TextAsset: Resources.Load<TextAsset>(\"SkylineAudio/hell-music/hell-music-manifest\"). Every 'resource' is a Resources path without extension (OGG Vorbis, 48 kHz stereo). 'status': ready = the file exists; pending = planned, not rendered yet (skip it, fall back as 'fallback' says). Times in seconds unless named _samples.",
  "sample_rate": 48000,
  "bus": "SkylineSoundCategory.Music",
  "cue_kinds": {
    "layered_loop": "Several stems of identical length that ALWAYS play together, sample-locked (schedule all with AudioSource.PlayScheduled on the same dspTime; re-schedule each pass at start + n*loop_samples/sample_rate, or use clip.loop=true on all of them started on the same dspTime). Mixing = per-stem gain only, never a restart.",
    "loop": "One file looping exactly at loop_samples (the whole file; tails are already folded onto the start).",
    "parts": "A cue made of named parts; each part is a loop or a stinger. Code switches parts on bar lines (bar_seconds) when the scene says so.",
    "stinger": "One-shot. Plays once; may overlap the music under it (duck the loop by duck_db for its length if given).",
    "oneshot": "A fitted piece that plays once from start to end."
  },
